Z||000003||theogre||02-26-2001||07:08 PM||||you replaced the module and coils so it's not likely them.<P>Like TG said check the wires are all on the right coils.<P>If you are sure teh wires and plugs are good check the crank pickup wiring. replace the crank pickup. If the pickup is bad it's going to feed a crappy signal to the moudule which will then feed crap to the ECM. Most places can't reliably test the sensor. resistance of the sensor is pretty meaningless as well.<P>that motor should also have a cam sensor on it. you need to make sure both are good.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 02-26-2001).]||||reg||1
